<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT - Lehman cuts Utd Biscuits.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Lehman cuts Utd Biscuits.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Biscuits (Holdings) Plc was cut to &quot;underperform&quot; from &quot;neutral&quot; by Lehman Brothers, which said the shares are trading at an undeserved premium to the market.</p>
<p>In a note, Lehman said it cut profit forecasts for 1997 when United Biscuits is not expected to benefit from exchange rates, while suffering from fierce competition in Australia.</p>
<p>Lehman has cut its 1997 profit estimate to 109.4 million stg from 123.9 million.</p>
<p>United Biscuits shares were unchanged at 250 pence.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
